 newly matched  edge pairs instead of just one or two as  in the beginner method so right now we  have one I have a green white piece and  I have another green white piece here  when we twist the top two centers to  match these green white pieces you'll  see that this piece here is going to  also go to the right so this one will  match up with this one and this piece  the blue yellow piece is going to come  over here so if we can get the other  blue yellow piece to be here when we  twist it we're going to make another  newly matched pair so that's how we  basically create the build ring we just  line them up three in a row basically so  we have one where's the other yellow  blue piece now so we look around the  cube and the other yellow blue piece is  over here so if we basically just turn  this all the way around it will be  aligned you're not going to be able to  match them up like that all the way  around the cube because it's going to  eventually interfere with the first one  so we have one edge pair here we have  another here and we could do one more so  it is the purple white piece where is  the other purple white piece it's right  here so we basically just need to align  it so if this piece needs to go over  here what we can do is we can twist it  down bring it up and then twist it back  and as you'll see these pieces are now  in the build ring so we have one edge  pair ready to be aligned two and three  so now what we do is we go to the first  one and we bring it over we basically  just slice the center's like we would to  match up the edge pairs when we do that  you'll see we have one two and three  there is basically only one edge pair  open here that is not going to be  matched okay so now what we need to do  is once we have them aligned and matched  we want to get them out of the way so we  can keep them the way they are we don't  want to lose these pieces which we just  aligned so we're going to be bringing  the center's back this way we're going  to be bringing blue back to blue yellow  back to yellow and so forth so as you'll  see this piece is going to go here when  we do that so if we can get the other  yellow red piece to be here on the  bottom that means that this will match  up with that piece so if we could find  that piece which is right here so  because this is on the top here it's in  the upper inside layer we want this  piece to be in the inner down layer so  we needed to be here so as you'll see it  is in the inner down layer here so if we  can get it to be here that will that  will be fine it will be in the build  ring so we bring it here and then we  bring this piece up now you'll see  they're opposite but they're not in the  building the building is going in this  direction so we have to fix the center's  like twisting it down and now these  pieces are in the building and as you'll  see that newly matched pair is in the  top layer so now this is going to be  brought this way so we have one and then  we have the blue white piece well  where's the other blue white piece the  other blue white piece is here so to get  it in the build ring we need it in the  lair here so what we can do is we  basically do the same thing we bring it  here we can bring this up and then we  realign the center so that these pieces  are now in the building then we have one  more so it is the green yellow piece  where is the other green yellow piece  the other green yellow piece is already  in the build ring as you'll see but it's  on the opposite side so what we do is we  basically just kick this piece out and  replace it with any unmatched pair and  now you'll see when we bring these  centers back these two pieces will be  aligned and you basically haven't lost  anything by doing that you'll have a  piece ready now to be matched up and as  you'll see we should now have six edge  pairs which have been matched so I hope  that helped you out and getting a little  bit quicker at the 4x4 cube it's  slightly different for the 5x5 cube but  you should be able to pick it up with  that as well
 

